<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring wheat bids mixed.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring wheat bids mixed.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring and white wheat bids were mixed on Monday and movement was slow as farmers wrapped up the wheat harvest, several cash grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Harvest is pretty much over and there's normally a lull immediately after,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said. &quot;They (producers) want to give prices a chance to improve.&quot;</p>
<p>Durum wheat prices jumped 20 to 50 cents per bushel as elevators scrambled to meet an August delivery requirement, one dealer said. He said the immediate shipment date carried a premium over September delivery.  </p>
